---
import ArrowIcon from '../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import SupportShell from '../components/SupportShell.astro';
import GuideScreenshot from '../components/GuideScreenshot.astro';
import GuideViewer from '../components/GuideViewer.astro';
import FooterIcon from '../components/FooterIcon.astro';
import Icon from '../components/HomeIcon.astro';
const screens=[
 {title:'01. Open the page you love.',src:'page',width:1230,height:908,screen:'Choose the original PDF',alt:'Actual Woodland Friends coloring page with PDF and Image download controls.',caption:'The PDF button on a real coloring page.',copy:'Open the full page, then choose PDF under “Print it. Keep it. Color it.” Collection cards offer the same PDF download. Use the full file rather than a thumbnail or screenshot.'},
 {title:'02. Download the print file.',src:'download',width:1120,height:837,screen:'The PDF download window',alt:'Actual download window with PDF selected, A4 description, file size and Download PDF.',caption:'A4 PDF selected in the actual download window.',copy:'Select PDF and choose Download PDF. Check the size or open File details, then find the saved document in browser downloads or your device Files app. Close the window to continue browsing.'},
 {title:'03. Match the paper. Preview first.',src:'print-details',width:504,height:706,screen:'A4 file information',alt:'Actual PDF file information showing A4, the download action and expanded file details.',caption:'A4 file information before you open your print settings.',copy:'Open the downloaded PDF in a viewer and choose Print. Select A4 and check the preview. Use Fit to printable area if edges are cropped, then print one test sheet. Your printer dialog may look different from these site screens.'}
];
---
<SupportShell title="How to Print Coloring Pages" description="A real coloring page, the right file and a clear path to paper. Follow the actual JotColoring screens, then check your printer’s preview." kind="help" eyebrow="FROM YOUR SCREEN TO PENCIL & PAPER">
 <div slot="hero" class="support-actions"><a class="support-button" href="#print-steps">See the real steps<ArrowIcon size={18}/></a><a class="support-button secondary" href="/how-to-use/">How to use JotColoring<ArrowIcon size={18}/></a></div>
 <GuideScreenshot slot="visual" hero src="/guides/walkthrough/download.webp" title="Your PDF is ready" alt={screens[1].alt} caption="Captured in the working download window." width={1120} height={837}/>
 <section class="walk-intro"><div><h2>A few minutes from page to paper.</h2><p>Catalog PDFs are A4 print documents with blank outlines and the JotColoring credit. Image downloads are WEBP files. Tap a screenshot below to see the real buttons and file information clearly.</p></div><FooterIcon name="printer" size={65}/></section>
 <div class="walk-print-flow" id="print-steps">{screens.map(s=><article><GuideScreenshot src={`/guides/walkthrough/${s.src}.webp`} title={s.screen} alt={s.alt} caption={s.caption} width={s.width} height={s.height}/><div><h2>{s.title}</h2><p>{s.copy}</p></div></article>)}</div>
 <div class="walk-checks"><div><Icon name="check" size={23}/><span><strong>Use the original file</strong><p>Small previews are for browsing. Download the PDF for the print document.</p></span></div><div><Icon name="check" size={23}/><span><strong>Keep every edge in view</strong><p>Match paper and orientation. Avoid borderless or oversize modes that crop the drawing or credit.</p></span></div><div><Icon name="check" size={23}/><span><strong>Choose supported paper</strong><p>Regular paper suits pencils and crayons. Follow your printer’s instructions before using heavier stock or wet coloring materials.</p></span></div><div><Icon name="check" size={23}/><span><strong>Start with one copy</strong><p>Check the complete outline, margins and your coloring materials before making several copies.</p></span></div></div>
 <section class="walk-step" id="colored-artwork"><div class="walk-step-copy"><span class="walk-step-no"><FooterIcon name="studio" size={36}/></span><h2>Printing something you colored?</h2><p>Open the project in Studio and choose Download or PDF. That export includes your colors. The collection PDF remains an uncolored original.</p><ol><li>Wait for Saved so the editable project is kept on this device.</li><li>Open the export flow and choose PDF.</li><li>Download the file, open it in a PDF viewer and check the print preview.</li></ol><div class="walk-tip"><FooterIcon name="help" size={26}/><span>A print file is not an editable backup. Keep a library backup separately to return to your layers or move a project to another browser.</span></div><a class="support-button" href="/my-artwork/">Open your saved artwork<ArrowIcon size={18}/></a></div><GuideScreenshot src="/guides/studio-export-v4.webp" full="/guides/studio-export-v4.webp" title="Export from Studio" alt="The real Studio download window with seven file formats and the colored artwork preview." caption="Save and export controls in the working Studio." width={1440} height={950}/></section>
 <section class="walk-two"><article><FooterIcon name="help"/><h2>If the print is not right.</h2><ul><li><strong>Cropped edges:</strong> check A4, orientation, scaling and Fit to printable area.</li><li><strong>Blurry lines:</strong> confirm you downloaded PDF rather than printing a small preview.</li><li><strong>The PDF did not open:</strong> check the saved file and try a current PDF viewer.</li><li><strong>Unexpected colors:</strong> use the catalog PDF for blank outlines, or Studio export for your painted version. The credit may be colored.</li></ul><a href="/help/">Get more help<ArrowIcon size={18}/></a></article><article><FooterIcon name="license"/><h2>For home or a classroom table.</h2><p>Personal and non-commercial educational use follows the Artwork license. Keep the JotColoring credit. Selling a workbook, product or file bundle requires written permission.</p><p>Need help with searching, coloring, saving or boards? Follow the full illustrated walkthrough.</p><a href="/how-to-use/">How to use JotColoring<ArrowIcon size={18}/></a><a href="/license/">Artwork license<ArrowIcon size={18}/></a></article></section>
 <GuideViewer/>
</SupportShell>
